<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian October export prices fall 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian October export prices fall 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian export prices fell 0.5 percent in October from the previous month and were 3.9 percent lower than in October 1995, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Lower world market prices led to decreases in the prices of cereals and aluminium,&quot; the bureau said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Partially offsetting these decreases were price increases for beef and petroleum,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The export price index bottomed in July with a fall in the annual rate of 7.6 percent and has been rising ever since.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
